WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:00.680


00:00.680 --> 00:01.360


00:01.360 --> 00:02.040


00:02.040 --> 00:02.720


00:02.720 --> 00:03.400


00:02.720 --> 00:03.400


00:02.720 --> 00:07.170
<b>Continuing with the national tournament finals, 
we have the Singles 1 match.</b>

00:05.130 --> 00:07.900
<b>The match between Rikkaidai Fuzoku's Yukimura Seiichi and...</b>

00:08.330 --> 00:09.570
Echizen.

00:08.610 --> 00:12.740
<b>Seishun Gakuen's Echizen Ryoma will begin momentarily.</b>

00:12.740 --> 00:14.410
<b>Both players to the court!</b>

00:13.150 --> 00:16.310
Hey, hey, Mr. Rikkai Captain.

00:16.310 --> 00:19.330
Before Koshimae gets here, how about a game with me?

00:19.660 --> 00:21.250
Please treat me favorably.{Let's play nice.}

00:24.500 --> 00:26.970
Shall we do it, Toyama-kun?{Let's do it then. Toyama-kun.}

00:33.380 --> 00:36.250
E-Excuse me, Ryoma-kun.

00:37.790 --> 00:39.820
I heard you lost your memory.

00:39.820 --> 00:43.810
You taught me tennis... {Literally: I have received tennise lessons from your before.}

00:44.820 --> 00:47.520
What are you talking about, Ryuzaki?

00:50.370 --> 00:51.940
Over there... is someone I absolutely must defeat.

00:51.940 --> 00:54.100
Over there... is someone I absolutely must defeat.

02:26.930 --> 02:29.410
U-Unbelievable.

02:29.860 --> 02:33.610
He won the game against an opponent like Toyama, who played evenly in a match against Echizen, {Against Toyama who is matched evenly in a game with Echizen, as an opponent.}

02:35.230 --> 02:38.230
with his jersey still on his shoulders.

02:39.720 --> 02:40.850
Kin-chan!

02:41.530 --> 02:42.590
Get a hold of yourself!

02:43.840 --> 02:45.560
The official records show...

02:45.980 --> 02:49.640
that Yukimura Seiichi has won every match he's ever played.{zensen zenshou = complete victories in all attempts}

02:49.640 --> 02:52.270
Moreover, not a single game has been taken from him.

02:52.270 --> 02:53.800
Not even one game?

02:54.320 --> 02:57.690
For his overwhelming victories, he was nicknamed...

02:58.670 --> 03:00.260
"The Child of God."

03:00.260 --> 03:01.980
Yukimura Seiichi.

03:02.610 --> 03:05.530
T-The Child of God.

03:13.330 --> 03:14.760
It looks like you've come.

03:33.920 --> 03:35.480
Thanks for waiting.

03:45.370 --> 03:47.420
You're late, Shorty. {I noticed that Ochibi was changed to Shorty in Episode 2. Tiny would be a more accurate as it refers to his small stature, not merely his height.}

03:47.420 --> 03:49.400
We were really worried about you.

03:49.400 --> 03:51.960
Geez, you got me all nervous.

03:53.060 --> 03:54.560
Sorry.

03:54.560 --> 03:55.880
Echizen.

03:58.610 --> 04:00.300
Everything you have,

04:00.300 --> 04:02.340
including what you've accumulated these past three and a half months... {even those accumulated from these three and a half months,}

04:02.340 --> 04:04.470
Unleash all of it in this match!

04:06.140 --> 04:07.390
Yup.{Is there a common translation for this?}

04:09.230 --> 04:12.350
He really lost his memory, right?

04:12.350 --> 04:15.430
But he somehow managed to capture the Spot.

04:15.430 --> 04:17.310
That was somewhat irritating.

04:18.640 --> 04:22.240
He actually broke through my Twist Spin Shot twice.

04:25.550 --> 04:27.120
Damn.

04:27.120 --> 04:29.450
I shouldn't have cooperated with them. {used this 協力kyouryoku- cooperate/ collaborate} {Alternatively: I shouldn't have agreed to help.}

04:34.750 --> 04:36.910
Start a new era...{Literally: Go change the era./ Change to a new era... }{時代jidai=era/ age/times}

04:36.910 --> 04:38.750
with your own strength. {With your own endeavors. }

04:43.230 --> 04:46.590
<b>The Singles 1 of the national tournament finals will now commence.</b>

04:46.590 --> 04:53.800
<b>The match between Rikkaidai Fuzoku's Yukimura Seiichi 
and Seishun Gakuen's Echizen Ryoma will now begin.</b>

04:55.330 --> 04:57.850
You're still recovering from an illness, right?

04:58.350 --> 05:00.220
It's better not to be so reckless then. {It's better not to push yourself too hard though. / It's better not to get too reckless.}{amari muri shina ho ga ii yo}

05:00.220 --> 05:01.720
That's a good look in your eyes. {Your eyes reflect your high spirits.}

05:03.760 --> 05:04.940
What's that?

05:04.940 --> 05:06.910
That's not much of an answer. {That doesn't answer my question.}

05:10.440 --> 05:12.040
Well, whatever.

05:13.200 --> 05:15.720
Echizen is taking this match too lightly. {I used 嘗めるnameru- put down, making light of}

05:15.720 --> 05:18.760
Well, he'll only be in high spirits now. {I used ikigaagatteiru 【意気が揚がっている】-to be in high spirits}

05:19.600 --> 05:20.630
Puri. {slang?}

05:21.630 --> 05:25.260
Seigaku has finally come this far.

05:25.260 --> 05:26.300
Yeah.

05:37.860 --> 05:39.600
Echizen-kun.

05:49.380 --> 05:51.070
Then I won't be holding back.

05:54.730 --> 05:57.660
A Twist Serve already!? {A twist serve all of a sudden?/ so abruptly?}

06:02.590 --> 06:04.500
This time it's the Drive A!

06:07.670 --> 06:08.780
Amazing!

06:08.780 --> 06:12.090
He's returning all of Echizen-kun's finishing moves.{He's returning all of Echizen's deciding shots.}

06:12.090 --> 06:12.890
That is...

06:14.490 --> 06:15.810
Cool Drive!

06:19.350 --> 06:20.440
0-15.

06:20.440 --> 06:22.160
He returned that so easily. {I heard : Anti kantan ni na. anti? deflect?}

06:22.160 --> 06:25.650
Moreover, he returned the shot precisely from the baseline.

06:28.240 --> 06:30.570
Not too bad, are you?

06:31.140 --> 06:33.450
However...

06:34.120 --> 06:37.010
Your jersey has fallen off your shoulders.

06:40.920 --> 06:42.040
I see.

06:42.470 --> 06:44.880
With the Twist Serve, he destroyed the opponent's setup. {taisei=set up/ preparations}

06:44.880 --> 06:47.530
He made him move both shoulders with the Drive A.

06:47.530 --> 06:49.930
Then the Cool Drive made him move forward.

06:50.350 --> 06:55.430
Just like that, he made the guy's jersey fall off naturally. {自明jimei= obvious/ evident/trivial. Instead of obviously, I used naturally}

06:56.950 --> 06:58.560
That's typical of Echizen.

06:58.560 --> 06:59.920
That's right.

06:59.920 --> 07:02.200
Echizen just has to be cheeky.{alternatively: It's Echizen to be cheeky after all.}

07:02.200 --> 07:03.990
Right, Inui-senpai?

07:03.990 --> 07:08.030
I-I'm just an observer from hell; a mysterious data soldier.{jigoku kara=from hell}{data senshi=data warrior/ soldier}

07:08.030 --> 07:10.580
What are you saying, Inui-senpai?

07:10.580 --> 07:11.920
Your cover is obviously blown. {bare bare desu}

07:16.200 --> 07:18.180
Thanks for your help, Sanada. {Sorry to have imposed on you, Sanada.}

07:19.080 --> 07:20.790
No need to thank me.

07:26.320 --> 07:27.560
Boy!

07:27.560 --> 07:30.470
This game isn't about falling jackets. {alternatively: otosu can be substituted with drop/ lose/let fall}

07:30.470 --> 07:31.590
Is that so? {Really?}

07:31.590 --> 07:33.590
So I won that game then. {So for that game, I won.}

07:35.770 --> 07:37.560
What a troublesome boy.

07:38.250 --> 07:39.710
This match is...{Alternatively: Mazui so kono shiai= This game is...unfavorable.}

07:39.710 --> 07:40.980
unfavorable.

07:41.390 --> 07:43.900
On top of having revealed all his special moves,

07:43.900 --> 07:47.210
his trump card, the Cool Drive, was ineffective.

07:50.660 --> 07:53.660
You still have lots more to work on.

07:53.660 --> 07:54.610
Here it comes.

07:54.610 --> 07:56.140
Muga no Kyouchi.

07:58.320 --> 07:59.540
Here I come then,

07:59.540 --> 08:01.100
Child of God.

08:03.830 --> 08:06.880
That is Tanishi-kun's Big Bang!

08:15.420 --> 08:18.350
There's power in that, but it's too simple.

08:21.690 --> 08:24.230
Now he's using Tachibana-san's Abare Dama. {Technique needs to be translated.}

08:24.780 --> 08:27.100
A ball doesn't replicate.

08:27.100 --> 08:28.360
In other words, there's only one ball. {Tsumari can be substituted with that is to say/ in short/ in brief}

08:32.400 --> 08:34.150
It's Chitose's Kamikakushi.

08:36.030 --> 08:38.490
The ball certainly did not disappear.

08:38.990 --> 08:40.910
That's not good, Echizen-kun.

08:40.910 --> 08:43.860
Yukimura can see through the techniques.

08:43.860 --> 08:45.670
The tactic he uses next is crucial.

08:47.580 --> 08:50.800
How long do you plan to carry on with this, boy? {How long are you planning to continue with this, boy?}

08:50.800 --> 08:54.970
Muga no Kyouchi will just drain your strength needlessly. { alternatively: Muga no Kyuochi will just waste your strength away. }

08:57.580 --> 09:00.330
You're quite a realist, aren't you?

09:05.090 --> 09:06.690
15-15.

09:06.690 --> 09:09.220
Ryoma-kun got a point back!

09:09.220 --> 09:10.650
All right, Echizen!

09:11.220 --> 09:13.730
Even FuuRinKaInZanRai's Lightning?

09:20.970 --> 09:22.130
You showed it to him?

09:23.700 --> 09:25.270
I told you.

09:25.270 --> 09:28.040
Take him head on and stand at the pinnacle. {pinnacle}

09:28.040 --> 09:31.880
That is our way of doing things at Rikkaidai Fuzoku.

09:40.370 --> 09:44.000
<i>Such things are merely childish sentiments. {Those are just some childish notion. }</i>

09:58.120 --> 10:01.660
<i>You got personal in a match and lost the Kantou District Tournament. {TLC}</i>

10:03.160 --> 10:04.080
<i>However...</i>

10:04.080 --> 10:08.300
<i>A match devoid of victory doesn't have an ounce{/ounce} of value!{...without victory...}</i>

10:16.960 --> 10:17.880
How naive!

10:17.880 --> 10:19.680
He returned the Lightning!?

10:28.030 --> 10:30.020
There's no dead space. {or blind spot. I used this 死角 shikaku}

10:33.010 --> 10:33.770
That is...

10:35.030 --> 10:39.700
Super Ultra Great Delicious Daisharin Yama Arashi! {Super ultra great delicious frenzied mountain storm!}

10:58.290 --> 11:00.930
H-He's strong!

11:01.520 --> 11:02.610
This is...

11:03.380 --> 11:05.160
Yukimura Seiichi?

11:19.110 --> 11:20.390
<b><i>Yukimura! Yukimura!</i></b>

11:20.390 --> 11:21.410
<b><i>Yukimura! Yukimura!</i></b>

11:21.410 --> 11:22.320
<b><i>Hurry up!{OR: Hurry up!}</i></b>

11:23.000 --> 11:25.990
<b><i>Hurry up and call an ambulance!{OR: Hurry up}</i></b>

11:30.520 --> 11:32.050
<b><i>Sorry.</i></b>

11:32.050 --> 11:36.540
<b><i>Without me, you'll have to battle in the Kantou District Tournament without a captain.</i></b>

11:36.540 --> 11:38.800
<b><i>Don't worry about it, Yukimura.</i></b>

11:38.800 --> 11:41.170
<b><i>For now, just give your undivided attention to your recovery.</i></b>

11:41.170 --> 11:43.250
<b><i>Rest assured. {Have a peace of mind.}</i></b>

11:43.250 --> 11:44.920
<b><i>Even without Captain Yukimura,</i></b>

11:44.920 --> 11:48.160
<b><i>Rikkai's third consecutive win will go without a hitch. {he said shikkaku wa nai= will not be disqualified. I used a more positive tone for this sentence. }</i></b>

11:48.160 --> 11:50.820
<b><i>When you put it like that, I feel somewhat depressed. {OR: When I hear it like that, it seems somewhat depressing.}</i></b>

11:50.820 --> 11:53.160
<b><i>What the heck are you saying?</i></b>

11:53.160 --> 11:56.400
<b><i>Well, I don't mean it that way.</i></b>

11:57.080 --> 11:58.640
<b><i>Apologize to the captain.</i></b>

11:58.640 --> 12:00.140
<b><i>Apologize right now.</i></b>

12:03.940 --> 12:04.700
<b><i>I was just kidding.</i></b>

12:04.700 --> 12:07.600
<b><i>Don't scare me like that, Captain. {Don't surprise / shock}</i></b>

12:07.600 --> 12:08.970
<b><i>That's true.</i></b>

12:09.600 --> 12:11.120
<b><i>Sanada.</i></b>

12:12.130 --> 12:13.250
<b><i>I'll leave it to you.</i></b>

12:14.120 --> 12:15.130
<b><i>Yes.</i></b>

12:15.690 --> 12:17.560
<b><i>With our power,</i></b>

12:17.560 --> 12:19.850
<b><i>we will definitely deliver the championship pennant to your hands. {we will definitely bring you the championship pennant.}</i></b>

12:26.270 --> 12:28.020
<b><i>About Yukimura-kun,</i></b>

12:29.010 --> 12:31.890
<b><i>with his body in such a state, he can no longer play tennis. {...,he will never play tennis again.}</i></b>

12:42.610 --> 12:44.410
<b><i>Sorry, Yukimura.</i></b>

12:45.700 --> 12:49.060
<b><i>But, at the upcoming national tournament, we'll definitely- {alternatively replace following with next/ upcoming}</i></b>

12:49.060 --> 12:50.570
<b><i>Will you please leave?</i></b>

12:51.620 --> 12:55.040
<b><i>I don't want to hear about what's next!{次Tsugi= next, following, subsequent}</i></b>

13:15.860 --> 13:17.820
<i>I then returned to the court. {After that, I came back on the court.}</i>

13:18.640 --> 13:22.190
<i>So that Rikkai's third consecutive win will be accomplished. {nashitogeru-to accomplish; to finish; to fulfill}</i>

13:29.550 --> 13:30.600
Echizen.

13:31.280 --> 13:32.750
This is bad.

13:32.750 --> 13:36.710
The continuous excessive use of techniques has drastically lowered his physical strength. {...has been tremendously drained.}

13:38.580 --> 13:39.870
What's the matter?

13:39.870 --> 13:41.420
Is that all you've got? {Are you done already?}

13:41.420 --> 13:43.900
This is where I want to be.{That's right where I want to be.}

13:48.930 --> 13:50.140
That is...

13:56.440 --> 13:58.690
Hyakuren Jitoku no Kiwami.

13:58.690 --> 14:00.020
There's still a long way to go.

14:03.600 --> 14:05.600
<i>The door that Tezuka Kunimitsu opened up,</i>

14:05.600 --> 14:09.740
<i>which is an adaptation of self-actualization's 
inner doors, is Hyakuren Jitoku no Kiwami. {OR: and adaptation of a state of self, Hyakuren Jitoku no Kiwami.}</i>

14:10.870 --> 14:14.430
<i>It's a state where all his power is concentrated in his left hand.</i>

14:14.430 --> 14:19.340
<i>It's a technique that minimizes fatigue and doubles the rotation of shots. {...with minimum weariness}</i>

14:20.790 --> 14:25.330
<i>In return, however, other reflexes become negligent.{However in relative to that, other course of actions becomes negligent. [careless]}</i>

14:25.330 --> 14:29.260
<i>Just like Tezuka, if{when} the zone is not perfectly formed, then...</i>

14:36.000 --> 14:37.810
15-40.

14:38.640 --> 14:40.730
...it's not much of a threat.

14:46.070 --> 14:47.860
Game, Rikkaidai Fuzoku.

14:47.860 --> 14:49.530
1-0.

14:50.700 --> 14:52.500
Game, Rikkaidai Fuzoku.

14:52.500 --> 14:53.990
2-0.

14:55.120 --> 14:56.870
Game, Rikkaidai Fuzoku.

14:56.870 --> 14:58.370
3-0.

14:58.890 --> 15:00.030
That's not working.

15:00.030 --> 15:03.910
No matter who he copies or what move he uses, it's ineffective. {TLC needed}

15:03.910 --> 15:05.600
Yukimura Seiichi.

15:06.510 --> 15:08.340
He's certainly the Child of God.

15:09.850 --> 15:11.820
It's probably too soon...

15:16.460 --> 15:18.570
for him to be where he is now. {used tadoritsuku- to struggle on to; to arrive somewhere after a struggle;}{alternatively: It's probably too soon for him to be where he is now.}{TLC needed}

15:24.420 --> 15:28.610
It's true that the freshman developed rather quickly. {...freshman grew too quickly.}{Tashikani = certainly/ surely}{"It's true" seems to be more appropriate here.}

15:28.610 --> 15:33.070
He has grasped the techniques perfectly of all the formidable opponents he has faced before.{...come across.}

15:33.070 --> 15:35.560
And that is on top of his exceptional natural talent. {..., he understood each of it completely.}

15:35.560 --> 15:37.390
Look at him.

15:37.390 --> 15:39.630
His Hyakuren is a good example.{His hyakuren has great spirit.}

15:39.630 --> 15:43.420
Even though he activated one of self-actualization's 
inner doors, it is completely out of his control. {OR: ...is completely being manipulated.}

15:46.580 --> 15:47.380
0-15.

15:48.310 --> 15:50.800
It's meaningless to continue with this.

15:50.800 --> 15:53.630
Losing quickly would be the best option for you.

15:54.600 --> 15:56.220
I'll definitely...

16:01.740 --> 16:04.520
I'll definitely make you gape in astonishment!

16:05.790 --> 16:07.090
Good grief.

16:07.090 --> 16:09.230
What an obstinate boy. {stubborn}

16:15.200 --> 16:16.470
Don't do it, Echizen!

16:16.470 --> 16:18.990
Hyakuren Jitoku has been seen through completely!

16:26.170 --> 16:29.090
He moved the aura of Hyakuren to his legs.

16:34.390 --> 16:35.930
Now it's in his right hand?

16:39.980 --> 16:41.060
Here it comes!

16:41.060 --> 16:43.270
Hyakuren Jitoku's double return!

16:56.730 --> 16:58.070
15-15.

16:58.070 --> 17:00.490
He's manipulating the aura at will.

17:00.490 --> 17:02.500
That's impossible.

17:05.920 --> 17:08.510
When the aura can be manipulated freely to where he wants it,   {tekizaitekisho 【適材適所】the right person in the right place }

17:08.510 --> 17:11.090
the burden on his body is alleviated significantly.

17:11.090 --> 17:14.510
The weakness of Hyakuren Jitoku has been overcome. {he said kokufuku=subjugation; conquest; victory : But I think these words are more appropriate here: conquered/ overcome}{The weakness of Hyakuren Jitoku has been overcome.}

17:19.260 --> 17:20.310
The next one...

17:20.930 --> 17:22.890
We'll finish it in six shots.

17:23.650 --> 17:25.560
<i>Now it's absolute prediction. {absolute prediction / insight}</i>

17:25.560 --> 17:27.620
<i>Saikikanpatsu no Kiwami, huh?{Pinnacle of great wisdom}</i>

17:32.440 --> 17:33.190
Two!

17:34.330 --> 17:35.070
Three!

17:38.320 --> 17:38.990
Four!

17:39.650 --> 17:43.410
<i>I certainly acknowledge this boy's latent abilities. {[OR] I certainly acknowledge this boy's latent abilities.}{I used: senzaiteki nouryoku- latent abilities.}</i>

17:43.410 --> 17:47.830
<i>Moreover, he has a will that never gives up in any adversity.</i>

17:48.450 --> 17:49.250
<i>But...</i>

17:49.250 --> 17:49.960
Five!

17:54.300 --> 17:55.340
Six!

18:02.390 --> 18:03.950
30-15.

18:03.950 --> 18:05.630
Echizen...

18:05.630 --> 18:07.560
missed a shot like that!? {Missed a shot like that!}

18:12.450 --> 18:13.540
Echizen!

18:13.540 --> 18:14.590
Shorty!

18:17.250 --> 18:19.220
<i>What?</i>

18:19.980 --> 18:21.310
<i>My body...</i>

18:21.710 --> 18:24.410
<i>My body won't move.</i>

18:24.410 --> 18:26.040
Is he all right?

18:28.330 --> 18:30.960
<i>If you were a mediocre player, {bonyou- mediocre, commonplace}</i>

18:30.960 --> 18:33.840
<i>you would never have to show such an unsightly form.</i>

18:34.500 --> 18:35.530
Shorty!

18:35.530 --> 18:38.420
What exactly happened there?

18:41.500 --> 18:43.190
Hey, are you all right?

18:45.470 --> 18:47.020
I'm fine.

18:47.020 --> 18:51.150
Geez! And after I called out six deciding shots too.

18:53.110 --> 18:54.150
Echizen!

18:54.150 --> 18:56.230
Are you really fine, Shorty!?

18:56.230 --> 18:58.170
Nosebleed! Nosebleed!

19:01.600 --> 19:02.870
It's true.

19:02.870 --> 19:04.950
I didn't notice it at all.

19:09.490 --> 19:10.490
What is it?

19:10.490 --> 19:12.390
It's not your fault or anything.

19:12.390 --> 19:14.210
From what I can see,

19:14.210 --> 19:16.840
you're practically losing your sense of touch, right?

19:32.900 --> 19:34.100
That's right.

19:34.100 --> 19:35.330
That's the one.

19:35.330 --> 19:36.430
That?

19:36.430 --> 19:37.980
What are you referring to, Kin-chan? {What are you referring to, Kin-chan?}

19:37.980 --> 19:39.220
Scary!

19:39.920 --> 19:41.760
It's truly scary.

19:41.760 --> 19:43.870
That guy's tennis, that is.

19:48.840 --> 19:49.660
It's about time.

19:51.930 --> 19:56.340
It's about time for Yukimura's true tennis to begin.

22:12.350 --> 22:15.050
To all the supporters, I give you my thanks. {I thank those who came to cheer for us.}

22:15.050 --> 22:18.070
It's unfortunate that it has to end at the finals. {TLC needed; original line was in past tense form}

22:18.070 --> 22:19.770
There's nothing to be sad about.

22:20.770 --> 22:21.860
Thank you, nya.

22:21.860 --> 22:25.230
The probability of meeting again is 95%.

22:25.230 --> 22:27.530
Thank you, baby!

22:27.530 --> 22:28.950
You guys are the best!

22:30.410 --> 22:31.420
I want a go at it!

22:32.160 --> 22:36.320
Next time: Dear Prince ~ To all the Princes of Tennis.

22:36.320 --> 22:38.940
We're going even higher.{We're going even further.}
